1. firmware/kv260-bitnet.bit.bin -- the FPGA bitstream
------------------------------------------------------

Generated with AMD Vivado Design Suite 2026.1 for the AMD XCK26 (Kria KV260 Vision AI Starter Kit,
part xck26-sfvc784-2LV-c) from the sources in hardware/.

It contains AMD LogiCORE IP in machine-executable form: the Zynq UltraScale+ MPSoC Processing
System (PG201), AXI DMA (PG021), AXI GPIO (PG144), AXI SmartConnect (PG247), AXI4-Stream Register
Slice (PG085) and Processor System Reset (PG164). Each of those product guides states that the
core "is provided at no additional cost with the AMD Vivado Design Suite under the terms of the
End User License", which is what section 3.1(3)A of that agreement requires of a "Core".

It is redistributed under section 3.1(3)C of the AMD/Xilinx End User License Agreement, which
permits distribution of Distributable Components that "have been converted into a machine
executable form, such as in the case of a Core or Design Element, a Bitstream", and under the same
section's requirement that "Distributable Components shall be distributed only for use to program
a Xilinx Device".

  It is supplied SOLELY for programming an AMD/Xilinx device -- specifically the XCK26 on a
  Kria KV260 -- and for no other purpose. Section 4(a) of that agreement forbids using a
  Bitstream to program or develop designs for non-AMD devices.

No .xci, .dcp, ip/ tree or synthesised IP netlist is shipped here: those would be Distributable
Components in Modifiable or Restricted form, for which the agreement's alternative limb applies and
a recipient would need their own Vivado licence. hardware/build-ffn.tcl regenerates all of them, so
