6. hardware/mul16.v
--------------------

The 16x16 multipliers in the FFN glue were not written by hand and are not from any third party:
they were grown by an evolutionary circuit compiler, assembled from sixteen partial-product pieces
it kept. They are original work under this repository's Apache 2.0 licence.

The provenance that stood in the file's own headers, kept here because the source carries no
comments: the modules pp00..pp15 and serial_add were emitted by `oracle netlist`, and in each of
them the line `always @(posedge clk or posedge rst)` was rewritten to `always @(posedge clk)`, so
rst is a synchronous clear. pp00..pp15 are the card-kept grids expeditions/mul/pp<i>fed.grid and
serial_add is expeditions/serial/planned.grid; mul16 composes them into a bit-serial 16x16
multiplier, a balanced tree four levels deep with a register on every node.

Nothing in hardware/ or runtime/ instantiates a Xilinx primitive -- no BUFG, XPM_, FDRE, RAMB or
DSP48 appears anywhere; the only vendor-specific text is the X_INTERFACE_INFO attribute strings,
which we wrote.
